title: Preserve failed validator incentive vesting payments instead of dropping them

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    When a vested payment to a validator cannot be added as a new System vesting schedule
    (because the per-kind slot cap is already full), the amount is merged into the existing
    System schedule whose ending block is closest to the incoming schedule's ending block.
    The target schedule's start and end blocks are preserved - only its locked amount and
    per-block rate are updated. This guarantees incentive payments are never lost.

    The `ValidatorIncentiveDropped` event is now reserved exclusively for non-recoverable
    failures (e.g. bonding duration of zero).

crates:
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-vesting
  bump: minor
